# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  EssentiElles — Backend configuration
#  Copy this file to `.env` and adjust values.
#  NEVER commit your real .env (it's git-ignored).
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# Database
# DB_BACKEND=mongodb  → production-grade MongoDB (requires MONGO_URL)
# DB_BACKEND=memory   → embedded in-memory DB for local tests/demos (no server needed)
DB_BACKEND=mongodb
MONGO_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017/
DB_NAME=livrella

# MongoDB Root Credentials (docker-compose only)
MONGO_ROOT_USER=admin
MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-me-please

# JWT — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=change-me-in-production-openssl-rand-hex-32
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
JWT_EXPIRY_DAYS=30

# Admin account (created automatically on first startup)
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@livrella.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=Admin2026!

# Application
ENVIRONMENT=development            # development | production
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Security
# Comma-separated list of allowed browser origins ("*" = everything, dev only)
CORS_ORIGINS=*
# Requests per minute per IP (0 = disabled)
RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=240

# Seed demo catalog/user on startup (true outside production by default)
SEED_DEMO_DATA=true

# Serve the static Expo web build (set the path to frontend/dist after
# `npm run build:web`) to serve API + web app from a single origin
WEB_DIST_DIR=

# Stripe payments (optional — demo mode stays active without these)
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_stripe_secret_key_here
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_your_webhook_secret_here
